      "1_2": "The Silk Road was a trade network. It linked China, India, and the west. Traders carried silk, spices, and ideas. This is cultural diffusion. Cultural diffusion is the spread of ideas, art, and technology. Buddhism spread from India to China this way.\n\nIn China, an empire ruled many lands. An empire has many territories under one ruler. Thinkers like Confucius shared a philosophy. A philosophy is a system of ideas about how to live.\n\nIn India, a monsoon is a seasonal wind that brings heavy rain.",
